flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the<br/>clamping arm bodies for cracks or bending<br/>deformation. 2. Check each pivot pin boss for<br/>looseness by attempting to rock the arm. 3. Inspect<br/>the clamping pad faces for wear beyond the minimum<br/>thickness."]
    box_2{"Cracks, deformation or severe wear on clamping arms?"}
    box_3(["End, Replace clamping unit: structural failure<br/>detected"])
    box_4["Place a calibrated load cell between the clamping<br/>pad face and a rigid reference block positioned at<br/>the nominal part contact surface height. Close the<br/>clamp to the production pressure setting and record<br/>the peak force from the load cell amplifier display.<br/>Repeat the measurement at all clamping stations and<br/>compare each reading against the minimum and maximum<br/>clamp force in the fixturing specification."]
    box_5[/"Refer to the clamping force specification."/]
    box_6{"Clamping force within ±5% of rated value?"}
    box_7["Replace return springs and check actuator seals"]
    box_8{"Reverify clamping force after spring replacement"}
    box_9(["End, Escalate: actuator servicing required, force<br/>unrecoverable"])
    box_10["Using a surface roughness tester, scan the clamp pad<br/>contact face in two perpendicular directions and<br/>record the Ra value. Compare against the maximum<br/>permitted roughness in the pad specification; an<br/>excessively rough pad will mark soft part materials.<br/>Using a calibrated surface plate and a dial gauge,<br/>measure flatness of the pad at four corner points<br/>and compare against the flatness tolerance."]
    box_11{"Clamp pad surface condition acceptable?"}
    box_12["Replace clamp pad, apply correct torque to retaining<br/>screws"]
    box_13["Command the clamp to the fully open position and<br/>measure the gap between the pad face and the<br/>reference surface using a digital caliper; compare<br/>against the nominal open position dimension. Close<br/>the clamp fully and probe the closed position sensor<br/>at its trigger point using a feeler gauge to measure<br/>the sensor actuation gap. Both values must fall<br/>within the tolerance ranges on the clamp setup<br/>drawing."]
    box_14[/"Refer to the clamping position tolerance."/]
    box_15{"Open and close sensor positions within ±0.3 mm of<br/>nominal?"}
    box_16["Reposition sensors and reteach open/close positions<br/>in programmable controller"]
    box_17{"Reverify sensor positions after reteach"}
    box_18(["End, Escalate: mechanical stop position shifted,<br/>datum check required"])
    box_19["Mount a dial test indicator against the pivot pin<br/>boss with the clamp arm loaded against its return<br/>spring. Measure the lateral displacement of the pin<br/>within the bore by applying a load perpendicular to<br/>the pin axis and recording the indicator reading.<br/>Compare the measured radial play against the maximum<br/>pin to bore clearance in the clamp specification;<br/>excessive play indicates worn pin or bore requiring<br/>replacement."]
    box_20{"Pivot pin radial clearance within 0.05 mm limit?"}
    box_21["Replace worn pivot pins and ream bore to H7<br/>tolerance"]
    box_22["Inspect each grease nipple on the pivot point<br/>assemblies for proper seating of the ball check<br/>valve by pressing the tip of a grease gun nozzle and<br/>confirming the nipple accepts grease. Apply two<br/>strokes of the specified grease grade to each<br/>nipple. Cycle the clamp arm through three full open<br/>and close strokes to distribute the lubricant before<br/>wiping excess from the pad face."]
    box_23[/"Refer to the clamping unit lubrication<br/>specification."/]
    box_24{"All pivot points correctly lubricated?"}
    box_25["Apply grease to all pivot pin nipples, quantity per<br/>spec"]
    box_26["Set the clamp controller to automatic cycle mode and<br/>command 20 consecutive open and close cycles at<br/>production speed. Monitor the cycle for consistent<br/>motion, absence of mechanical shock at end of<br/>stroke, and correct sensor signals at each position.<br/>Record the cycle time and compare against the target<br/>cycle time; an increase greater than 15% indicates<br/>hydraulic or pneumatic system degradation."]
    box_27{"All 20 cycles completed without missed clamp or<br/>timeout?"}
    box_28["Investigate cycle fault, check sensor and actuator<br/>timing"]
    box_29["Complete the following steps: 1. Load the reference<br/>part into the fixture and close the clamp to<br/>production pressure. 2. Attempt to move the<br/>reference part by applying a lateral force by hand.<br/>3. Confirm the part does not move and record the<br/>clamping force reading."]
    box_30{"Reference part held without movement during<br/>simulated cut?"}
    box_31["Log clamp force and cycle data, update service<br/>record"]
    box_32(["End, Procedure complete"])
    box_33["Secondary spring set replacement: remove all<br/>clamping springs and verify the spring seat surfaces<br/>are clean and undamaged before fitting. Install new<br/>springs from the correct specification batch,<br/>confirming the free length of each spring matches<br/>the specification before installation. Cycle the<br/>clamp five times after replacement to allow the<br/>springs to seat before returning to the clamping<br/>force measurement step."]
    box_34[/"Fixture datum and locating diagnostic (GRAPH 44)"/]

